  "body": "### Description\n\nLogin API `https://matrix-client.matrix.org/_matrix/client/v3/login` presents login via `m.login.application_service` also if no [`app_service_config_files`](https://matrix-org.github.io/synapse/latest/usage/configuration/config_documentation.html#app_service_config_files) is configured.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- setup a new homeserver\r\n- request `/_matrix/client/v3/login`\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n   \"flows\":[\r\n      {\r\n         \"type\":\"m.login.password\"\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n         \"type\":\"m.login.application_service\"\r\n      }\r\n   ]\r\n}\r\n```\n\n### Homeserver\n\nanother\n\n### Synapse Version\n\n1.78.0\n\n### Installation Method\n\nDocker (matrixdotorg/synapse)\n\n### Database\n\nPostgreSQL\n\n### Workers\n\nMultiple workers\n\n### Platform\n\nK8s\n\n### Configuration\n\n_No response_\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nNone\n```\n\n\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\n\nProbably there could be a check here for app services:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/98fd558382226b347d78e5f6e6782c6e74c25e69/synapse/rest/client/login.py#L170",
